  "document": "J.B. Scott's\nJ.B. Scott's was a nightclub located on Central Avenue in Albany, New York. Its capacity was approximately 700. It was open from 1979 to 1982 when it burned down. Its performers included U2, John Mellencamp, Bryan Adams, Thin Lizzy, Pat Benatar and Iggy Pop. In 1985 club owner Douglas Jacobs opened another nightclub in Albany named J.B.'s Theatre."
